# PLAN-968 T-02/T-03 — permanent M2-A task actor & event scheduler corpus:
# `task`/`on` declarations, `Task.spawn`, handle `send`/`ask`/`stop`,
# `reply`, `await`, `go`, `sleep`, bounded mailboxes (backpressure),
# virtual timers, the orderly stop-hook drain and named rejections, all
# on `ac-av/scheduler-source-run-v1` (the deterministic cooperative
# scheduler; console stdout observed byte-exactly). The canonical
# `message_handler`/`spawn_with_state` obligations are the originals,
# unmodified. Unit-level oracles also live in `ace-av`
# (`sched_m2_968`).

```test-case
case {
  schema: "autolang.case/2", id: "ace.m2.p968.message-handler", tags: ["ace-m2", "scheduler", "plan-968"], links: ["PLAN-968"],
  source: { file: "src/message_handler.at", syntax: "auto", path: "main.at" }, entry: { mode: "program" },
  checks: [{ id: "av-scheduler", adapter: "probe", action: "run",
    options: { recipe: "ac-av/scheduler-source-run-v1", av: { entry: "d_main" }, steps: [{ op: "run" }] },
    expect: { completion: "success", exit: 0, stdout: { text: "got one\n", compare: "bytes" }, stderr: { text: "", compare: "bytes" } } }]
}
```

